# Shipped Agent Documentation

`Version Control.accda.src/AGENTS.md` and `Version Control.accda.src/vcs-agent-docs/*.md`
are embedded as resources and extracted into **every user's export folder on every
export**. They are read by an agent working in somebody else's Access database, and
they occupy that agent's context on every turn.

They are budgeted: **150 lines for the entry `AGENTS.md`, 110 for each reference**.
`modTestAgentDocs` fails the build when a budget is exceeded, a reference is not
linked from the entry file, a repo-relative link appears, or a document is missing
from `modResource.GetAgentDocFiles`.

Before adding anything to them, read
[docs/agent-docs-maintenance.md](../../docs/agent-docs-maintenance.md) — it carries
the gate for deciding whether a change belongs there at all, the routing table for
which file it goes in, and the list of things that must never ship (add-in
internals, repo-relative paths, examples taken from this repo, changelog voice).

The root `AGENTS.md` is a different audience — contributors to this repository —
and is not subject to those rules.
